# For the DEVELOPER, not for users. Copy to `.env` (git-ignored) and fill in; the build reads it
# (src-tauri/build.rs) and bakes the client into the app, so users only click "Sign in with
# Google" and never see or enter credentials. Environment variables of the same name win over
# this file (use that in CI).
#
# Google OAuth client for Drive sync (spec 22, ADR-0011). Create it in the Google Cloud Console:
# enable the Google Drive API, then Credentials -> OAuth client ID -> type "Desktop app".
# Minimap asks only for the drive.file scope. Google treats a desktop app's secret as
# non-confidential, but keep it out of git anyway.
#
# Rebuild after changing them. A build without them shows an "Advanced" box in Settings where
# a developer can paste a client for testing; a build WITH them hides that box.
MINIMAP_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
MINIMAP_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
